    "topicLabel": "Stability Factor and Collector Current",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "A biasing circuit has a stability factor of 40. If due to temperature change, IB changes by 1 μA. Then the change in IC will be",
    "options": [
      "20μA",
      "40μA",
      "80μA",
      "none of these"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Stability factor S = ΔIC/ΔIB. Therefore: 40 = ΔIC/1 μA → ΔIC = 40 μA",
