    "topicLabel": "Shear Stress in Tension",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "A bar of square section is subjected to a pull of 10,000 kg. If the maximum allowable shear stress on any section is 500 kg/cm², then the side of the square section will be",
    "options": [
      "5 cm",
      "√10 cm",
      "15 cm",
      "20 cm"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "For maximum shear stress on a plane at 45°: τ_max = P/(2A). Therefore 500 = 10000/(2a²), giving a² = 10, so a = √10 cm",
    "source": "MPSC (Mizoram)",
    "year": 2015,
