    "subject": "gk",
    "topic": "real-analysis-continuity",
    "topicLabel": "Real Analysis - Continuity",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Consider the real function f(x) = {1 if x is rational, 0 if x is irrational}. Then",
    "options": [
      "f is discontinuous at every point",
      "f is continuous at every point",
      "f is discontinuous on R except at origin",
      "None of these"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "This is Dirichlet's function, discontinuous at every point in R. At any point, every interval contains both rational and irrational numbers, so the function oscillates between 0 and 1, violating continuity.",
