    "subject": "gk",
    "topic": "hilbert-spaces-lp-spaces",
    "topicLabel": "Hilbert Spaces and L^p Spaces",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The space l^p is a Hilbert space if",
    "options": [
      "p = 1",
      "p = 2",
      "p = 3",
      "p = n"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Only l^2 is a Hilbert space because it is the only l^p space where the norm is induced by an inner product. The inner product <x,y>=sum(x_i*conj(y_i)) generates the l^2 norm. For p≠2, l^p spaces are Banach spaces but not Hilbert spaces.",
