    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The position of a particle moving along a straight line is defined by the relation, x = 2t³ – 12t² - 40t + 50, where 'x' is in meters and 't' in second. The acceleration of a particle at t = 2 sec is:",
    "options": [
      "0",
      "12 m/sec²",
      "24 m/sec²",
      "36 m/sec²"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Acceleration a = d²x/dt² = d/dt(6t² - 24t - 40) = 12t - 24. At t = 2 sec: a = 12(2) - 24 = 24 - 24 = 0 m/sec².",
    "source": "MPSC (Mizoram)",
    "year": 2016,
    "tags": [
      "kinematics"
    ],
    "paperId": "mpsc-cli-1-ae-sdo-2016-under-pwd-civil-engineering-paper-i",
