    "topicLabel": "Water Balance Equation",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The formula I = O + ΔS, where I = inflow, O = outflow, and S = change in storage, is used for expressing:",
    "options": [
      "Hydrologic equation",
      "Water balance equation",
      "Evapotranspiration",
      "Infiltration in a given area"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "This is the water balance equation (also called the hydrologic equation or continuity equation), which states that inflow equals outflow plus the change in storage over a given area and time period.",
