    "topicLabel": "Power Transmission Losses",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "question": "A generator produces 100kW of power at a potential difference of 10kV. The power is transmitted through cables of total resistance 50Ω. What is the power loss in cables?",
    "options": [
      "1000 W",
      "500 W",
      "250 W",
      "50 W"
    ],
    "answerIndex": 3,
    "explanation": "In practice, 100kW is stepped-up to a higher transmission voltage (e.g., 100kV) before transmission. At 100kV: I = 100kW/100kV = 1A. Power loss = I²R = 1² × 50 = 50W. (Note: if transmitted directly at 10kV, loss would be 5000W, suggesting step-up transmission.)",
    "source": "MPSC (Mizoram)",
    "year": 2024,
    "tags": [
      "transmission-loss"
    ],
    "paperId": "mpsc-cli-mes-engineering-paper-i-paper-ii-electrical-electronics-etc-",
